<title>UK: UK independent forecasts show end-97 rates over 7%.</title>
<headline>UK independent forecasts show end-97 rates over 7%.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Official British interest rates are expected to rise above 7.0 percent in the fourth quarter of 1997 from the present 6.0 percent, according to the latest summary of independent forecasts compiled by the Treasury.</p>
<p>The average of forecasts compiled from independent and City institutions in the three months to December was 7.17 percent and the range was 5.80 to 8.15 percent.</p>
<p>Following are key forecasts from the Treasury compilation (annual percentage changes unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>    AVERAGE OF NEW FORECASTS		    1996	1997</p>
<p>    GDP						  2.4	3.5</p>
<p>    RPI  (Q4)					  2.6	3.5</p>
<p>    RPIX (Q4)					  3.2	3.0</p>
<p>    Unemployment (Q4, millions)		  2.02     1.81</p>
<p>    Current account deficit (bln stg)	  1.4	4.2</p>
<p>    PSBR (bln stg)				  26.4     20.9</p>
<p>    Interest rates (Q4)			    6.14     7.17</p>
<p>NOTE: RPI is retail price index. RPIX is retail price index exclusing mortgage interest payments (underlying inflation).</p>
<p>PSBR is public sector borrowing requirement (budget deficit) and estimates are for the financial year to April 5.</p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
